# ─── LAUNCHER SCRIPTS ARE SOURCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The blanket *.bat / *.ps1 rules above exist to keep throwaway scratch scripts out of
# the repo. They also swallowed the platform's own entry points, so start_model.bat and
# tools/start_model.ps1 could not be committed at all (found 2026-11-13 when git add
# refused them). These are the files that start and stop the platform -- they belong in
# history, because "how it is deployed" is part of what was measured.
!START_TRM_PLATFORM.bat
!STOP_TRM_PLATFORM.bat
!start_model.bat
!tools/*.ps1
# tools/*.bat are the platform's own launchers (start_embedder_8593, start_vote_model_8587), not
# scratch scripts. They were landing in the blanket *.bat rule and had to be `git add -f`'d, which
# means a launcher that only exists on this disk is not reproducible. Keep them in history.
!tools/*.bat

# --- training environment -------------------------------------------------
# 2.1 GB / 23,161 files measured on 2026-11-15, zero of them tracked in git.
# Left inside the repo it was 68.7% of every code file in the tree (G150), which made any
# "how much code is this?" count meaningless. Recreate with `python -m venv train_venv`.
train_venv/


# G161: generated artifacts that must never be versioned (no inline comments - gitignore takes
# them literally, which is how the ledgers stayed in the tree)
swarm_v2_artifacts/CADENCE_LEDGER*.jsonl
data/turbo_memory_index.jsonl
data/embed_progress.jsonl
data/kanban_board.json.bak-*
swarm_v2_global_memory/fabric/*.bak-*

